# Changelog

All notable changes to `@re-cinq/hal-engine` are documented here.

The format is [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres to
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html). Entries are written for somebody installing the
package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.

## [Unreleased]

### Changed

- Rejected tool inputs now log the failing field and schema constraint without logging the rejected value.

- Tools with dynamic definitions now validate each call against the current input schema, reusing validators when the schema object is unchanged.

- Static tools now return schema validation failures as tool results before their executor runs. Executors no longer receive malformed input rejected by their declared schema.

- Static tool definitions now fail registration immediately when their JSON Schema cannot be compiled. The error names the tool, so configuration mistakes can be corrected at startup.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17

### Changed

- `HalEngineConfig.orchestrator.hooks` now carries a JSDoc comment. The field already shipped
  in `0.2.x`; the comment makes the lifecycle-hook seam discoverable from the published type
  declarations so editors surface it on hover without a trip to the README.

